    "result_text": "All 286 tests pass, including the new `Cp19Tests`.\n\nI implemented the change in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, the endpoint that handles owner creation:\n\n- Added a dedicated `AUDIT` logger: `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- After a successful `saveOwner`, it logs at INFO the authenticated user (from the Spring Security context), the new owner's id, and membership number:\n  ```\n  AUDIT - Owner created by user=acceptance-admin ownerId=11 membershipNumber=11\n  ```\n- Added a small `currentUsername()` helper that reads the authenticated principal from `SecurityContextHolder`, falling back to `\"anonymous\"` when unauthenticated.\n\nThe log line is emitted only on the success path (after all validation/limit/duplicate checks and the save), so rejected creations are not audited.",
